Overview

The Chronos‑State Bifurcation Engine is a unified scientific simulation architecture designed to explore physically plausible alternate futures of planetary systems. It integrates:

planetary physics solvers

chaotic state‑space evolution

cryptographic provenance

dual‑timeline simulation

attractor‑basin mapping

SSIM‑based physical validation

This framework introduces a new class of multi‑timeline modeling for planetary science, chaos theory, and high‑performance computational physics.

